course: dictionary
lesson: 12045
title: Going all the way round
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A circumnavigation is a journey all the way around something. Look at the word in pieces: circum means around, and navigation means finding your way and travelling by sea or air. So a circumnavigation is a trip that goes around the whole of something, such as the world. «Magellan's crew made the first circumnavigation of the world.» The crew sailed all the way around the Earth, not just across the sea.
explain: Clues in the sentence help you. «Their circumnavigation took nearly three years.» A trip that takes years is a very long journey, so it must be a long way around. «The pilot planned a circumnavigation of the globe by plane.» Globe tells you the journey goes around the whole Earth, and by plane tells you it is in the air.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The pilot planned a journey all the way around the globe by plane.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits. Now try «The pilot planned a short walk to the shop.» That does not fit a circumnavigation, so the word must mean something much bigger.
fact: Circum means around, as in circle and circumference.
fact: «Circumnavigation» means a journey all the way around something, especially the world by sea or air.
fact: Magellan's expedition, finished by Elcano, made the first circumnavigation of the world, from 1519 to 1522.
fact: Francis Drake made a circumnavigation from 1577 to 1580.
fact: A circumnavigation of the Earth around the equator is about 40,000 km.
exercise: «The sailors made a circumnavigation of the world.» What is a circumnavigation? | A big storm at sea | A map of the ocean | *A journey all the way around something | A short trip to the harbour and back
exercise: In the word circumnavigation, which part means around? | sea | trip | *circum | globe
exercise: Francis Drake made a circumnavigation in the 1500s. In which years did his voyage happen? | 1800 to 1805 | 1900 to 1910 | *1577 to 1580 | 1519 to 1522
test: «The first circumnavigation of the Earth was finished by Elcano's crew.» What does circumnavigation mean here? | A sea map showing the coast | A short river trip | A fight between two ships | *A journey all the way around the world
test: About how far is a circumnavigation of the Earth around the equator? | About 4,000 km | About 400,000 km | About 400 km | *About 40,000 km
exam: Which sentence uses circumnavigation correctly? | She has a circumnavigation of blue eyes. | They ate a circumnavigation for their lunch. | The circumnavigation was a very loud song. | *They planned a circumnavigation of the globe by plane.
